    "body": "> > to change the remove version variable to remove the `v` as you suggested\n> \n> that I'd even be able to help with as it seems like a simple search&kill operation in one file per module (plus a similar fix in the test section)...\n> \n> > but then also update the default format string to include the `v` something like `\"${symbol}(v${version} )\"`.\n> \n> Is this also a similarly simple search&replace operation in the corresponding module [config file](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/configs/python.rs#L24)? \n> ```rust\n>             format: \"via [${symbol}${pyenv_prefix}(${version} )(\\\\($virtualenv\\\\))]($style)\",\n> ```\n> Or is it more complicated and then I can't really help as I know no 🦀 :(\n\nYep, that would be the bulk of the work along with updating the docs. Some of the modules might be a bit trickier, python is one because it supports using the pyenv name rather than the version but so we might need to think about it a bit more. ",
