    "body": "> Yep, that would be the bulk of the work along with updating the docs. Some of the modules might be a bit trickier, python is one because it supports using the pyenv name rather than the version but so we might need to think about it a bit more.\r\n\r\nAlso managed to partially fix this by adding an extra variable for the pyenv version number so that you could have different prefixes for each and avoid `🐍 test_pyenv vsystem` in the pyenv case while still having `🐍 v3.8.2` for the regular python version\r\nAlthouh this would also preclude `🐍 test_pyenv v3.8.2`, but since I don't really need the `v` and also don't understand what's required to make it work both for the `system` and numeric pyenv versions, will definitively leave it to someone more knowledgeable",
